			"text": "Melanedaphodon was a synapsid that lived in Carboniferous North America, discovered in the Allegheny formation of Pennsylvania. Its name means 'Black Pavement Tooth'. It was a small edaphosaur, having the common sail of its relatives. Thanks to its teeth, it's been thought that this animal was an omnivore. Feeding on both animal matter and low-fibre plants."
